@flexiarg operator/route-work-to-another-agent-family-because-one-pool-is-low
@title Route Work To Another Agent Family Because One Pool Is Low
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 6 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade; THEN worded 5 ways across its proposals
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-5p0cAT turn-G1cBQ0 turn-N1UMLv turn-Q2zTT7 turn-dHojgw turn-uI3rNy
@parent agent/handoff-preserves-context
@context One agent family's usage is out or running low.

! conclusion: Use the named families and do not fall back to the low one; say if the task cannot be done that way.

  + IF:
    The operator says which families to use for the helpers instead.

  + HOWEVER:
    The roster decides which seats are actually free, and a fallback to the low pool would spend what the operator wants kept.

  + THEN:
    Use the named families and do not fall back to the low one; say if the task cannot be done that way.

  + BECAUSE:
    The operator is protecting a scarce usage window or avoiding a dead one.
